            <ArticleTitle>Transient bone marrow oedema syndrome: a report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>335-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transient bone marrow edema syndrome (TBMES) is a disorder with unknown etiology and must be included in the differential diagnosis of hip pain. TBMES generally has a good prognosis but, it can be result in avascular necrosis (AVN). We present two cases diagnosed with TBMES, one of whom experienced full remission and the other who developed AVN.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
